Original commit body from f566fa883c88477ed42935e61680323762983d73:

Drains 43 type-arg errors across three self-contained modules. Removing
them REVEALED 37 others across four codes, and every one was real. Four
measure-fix rounds to converge; net -44.

WHAT THE BARE GENERICS WERE HIDING:

  * `list` is INVARIANT. A TaintSource|TaintSink union alias -- correct
    about what flows through -- was wrong about the container: the helpers
    only READ, so they take Sequence/Mapping and now accept a concrete
    list[TaintSource] at every call site.
  * One function bound `edge` to a DdgEdge in two loops and to a
    call-edge DICT in three more. Invisible while both were Any; the two
    DDG loops are renamed, since sharing a name across two element types
    is what let the ambiguity hide.
  * _merge_with_user_override is TYPE-PRESERVING -- hand it sources, get
    sources back. A union return would have let a merged source+sink
    mapping be assigned onto a sources-only catalog field, so it carries a
    TypeVar bound to the union instead.
  * One dict genuinely holds two nested summaries plus an int count, and
    inference narrowed it the moment to_dict() was typed.

THE PATTERN, which changes the estimate for the rest of the drain: a bare
dict/list is not laziness, it is LOAD-BEARING AMBIGUITY. The sites hardest
to annotate are exactly the sites where the code is polymorphic and the
bare generic let nobody decide. Three of the reveals were our own
annotations being wrong, each caught by the whole-tree ratchet before
reaching a PR. So the remaining ~360 type-arg errors are a LOWER bound on
the work, not an upper one, and the drain is not monotonic.

Types are measured, not assumed: list[Edge] where the body does attribute
access (edge.meta / edge.dst) versus dict[str, dict[str, Any]] where it
subscripts (node.get("meta")) -- both in ONE signature in
_compute_external_potential, which is what a blanket rule gets wrong.
Cross-module references (DdgEdge from cfg, Edge from ir) are TYPE_CHECKING
imports: no cycle exists either way, but the runtime import graph stays
unchanged for modules the CLI loads on every invocation.

Baseline ratcheted 1036 -> 992. 3539 tests pass, scoped coverage clean.

